# Rot-Curse Rakshasa has decayed, whose "this creature can't block" (CR 702.147a, 509.1b) keeps it out of Bot1's blocks:
# when Bot2's Embereth Shieldbreaker attacks on turn 4, the Rakshasa may not block it, and Bot1's Cecil, Dark Knight (the
# positive control) may and does. Cecil's deathtouch kills the Shieldbreaker; Cecil's Darkness ability makes Bot1 lose the
# 2 Cecil dealt. The Rakshasa never attacked, so it is still on the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Rot-Curse Rakshasa
Cecil, Dark Knight
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rot-Curse Rakshasa.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cecil, Dark Knight.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Embereth Shieldbreaker > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Rot-Curse Rakshasa > Embereth Shieldbreaker)
Bot1.Block(Cecil, Dark Knight > Embereth Shieldbreaker)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Embereth Shieldbreaker
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Mox Jet; Rot-Curse Rakshasa; Cecil, Dark Knight
Bot1.Battlefield.Rot-Curse Rakshasa.Keywords = Decayed; Trample
